<BaseLayout title="Asset licence and permitted uses | 88cutouts" description="Personal-use permissions for 88cutouts downloads, redistribution limits, commercial enquiries and rights concerns.">
  <div class="wrap"><article class="prose">
    <h1>Asset licence</h1>
    <p>Last updated 26 September 2026. This page explains the personal-use permission offered for downloads from 88cutouts. A file being available online does not put it in the public domain.</p>
    <h2>Personal projects</h2>
    <p>You may download assets and resize, rotate, crop or combine them for your own personal social posts, private messages, notes, wallpapers, school projects and cards for friends. Attribution is appreciated but not required by 88cutouts for these uses.</p>
    <h2>Redistribution and resale</h2>
    <p>Do not sell the files, redistribute the library, upload the assets to a stock service, or package them as a competing downloadable collection. Link to the original page when sharing an asset with someone who wants their own copy.</p>
    <h2>Commercial use</h2>
    <p>Personal-use permission does not cover client work, business promotions, merchandise or paid templates. Contact <a href="mailto:hello@88cutouts.com">hello@88cutouts.com</a> with the exact asset URL and proposed use. Obtain written permission before proceeding; sending an enquiry is not permission.</p>
    <h2>Other rights</h2>
    <p>These terms cover only permissions 88cutouts is entitled to grant. They do not grant rights in third-party brands, a person's likeness, or material you add to a composition. Keep the licence and source information for your own photos and other inputs.</p>
    <h2>Rights concerns</h2>
    <p>If you believe a download includes your work without permission, use our <a href="/contact/#rights">rights-reporting instructions</a>. Include the asset address and information identifying your original work so it can be investigated.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href="/terms/">website terms</a> and <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
